      "translations": {
        "en": "(The Manifest) The meaning of al-Zahir is that He is manifest through His signs, which He displayed as witnesses of His power, traces of His wisdom, and evidence of His proof, which all creation is unable to create the smallest of, or produce the easiest of, in their eyes, as Allah said: 'Surely those whom you call upon besides Allah cannot create a fly, though they should gather for it' (3). Therefore, nothing in His creation is not a witness to His Oneness from all its sides. He, the Blessed and Exalted, avoided describing His Essence (4), so He is manifest through His signs and witnesses of His power, hidden by His Essence. A second meaning is that He is Manifest, Overpowering, and Capable of what He wills. From this is His word: 'And they became uppermost,' i.e., predominant over them. (The Hidden) The meaning of al-Batin is that He is hidden from imaginations. He is Hidden without encompassment. Nothing encompasses Him because He preceded thought, so thought was subject to Him (1). The Known preceded, so it did not encompass Him (2). It escaped imaginations, so they did not explore Him. Eyes wandered from Him and did not perceive Him. He is the Hidden of all Hidden, the Veil of all Veils. He is Hidden in Essence, and Manifest and Exalted in Signs. He is the Hidden without a veil and the Manifest without approximation. A second meaning is that He is the Interior of everything, i.e., All-Knowing and All-Seeing of what they keep secret and what they disclose, and of whatever He sowed and created. The entourage of a man is his close people who enter into his personal affairs. The meaning is that He is All-Knowing of their secrets, not that He, the Mighty and High, hides in a thing disguising in it."
